1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,640
Robots learn from human demonstrations, and the people

2
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:06,578
who record them are rarely paid or credited.

3
00:00:06,608 --> 00:00:10,618
Thenar is for them: drive a robot arm from a browser, a

4
00:00:10,648 --> 00:00:15,006
Quest or a leader arm, and get paid on Monad for every run.

5
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,561
The other side is a robotics lab.

6
00:00:18,591 --> 00:00:22,020
Its budget is a Privy server wallet whose policy only

7
00:00:22,050 --> 00:00:26,177
lets it fund Thenar. It posts a bounty on Monad, and

8
00:00:26,207 --> 00:00:29,103
when it's asked to send money anywhere else, Privy

9
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:30,588
refuses to sign.

10
00:00:31,268 --> 00:00:35,243
An operator signs in. Each onboarding step is read from the chain.

11
00:00:35,923 --> 00:00:38,539
A passkey makes them a person on chain.

12
00:00:38,569 --> 00:00:41,481
Monad's P-256 precompile verifies it through

13
00:00:41,511 --> 00:00:42,963
PasskeyRegistry.

14
00:00:43,643 --> 00:00:46,074
With Mera, the same passkey derives the key that

15
00:00:46,104 --> 00:00:47,432
commands their arm.

16
00:00:48,643 --> 00:00:51,887
Now the lab's task, in WebXR, with an emulated Quest

17
00:00:51,917 --> 00:00:53,546
standing in for the headset.

18
00:00:54,226 --> 00:00:57,017
Squeeze to take the arm, and it follows the controller

19
00:00:57,047 --> 00:00:58,689
millimetre for millimetre.

20
00:00:58,719 --> 00:01:02,148
Grip the payload, carry it over, and set it in the ring.

21
00:01:14,226 --> 00:01:15,182
In tolerance.

22
00:01:17,226 --> 00:01:20,238
Submit. The verifier scores the samples and signs, and

23
00:01:20,268 --> 00:01:23,151
one transaction records the run and pays the operator.

24
00:01:23,831 --> 00:01:28,111
Executed 1.09 s after the send, and final at 1.21 s, on

25
00:01:28,141 --> 00:01:31,626
Monad testnet, measured in this browser.

26
00:01:31,656 --> 00:01:33,761
The receipt shows every step:

27
00:01:33,791 --> 00:01:38,381
seen by the node, executed, then final, checked against

28
00:01:38,411 --> 00:01:39,926
the finalized tag.

29
00:01:40,606 --> 00:01:43,327
And the operator now owns shares of this corpus.

30
00:01:44,106 --> 00:01:48,081
The run is now data, built from the samples its hash commits to.

31
00:01:52,106 --> 00:01:55,002
An AI agent buys it over x402:

32
00:01:55,032 --> 00:01:58,321
one cent of USDC, settled on Monad.

33
00:01:58,351 --> 00:02:03,093
Then it checks the file against the sale logged on chain.

34
00:02:03,773 --> 00:02:05,797
The terms, and every sale, are public.

35
00:02:09,773 --> 00:02:12,587
Chainlink CRE then audits the corpus.

36
00:02:12,617 --> 00:02:16,546
It rebuilds each task's Merkle root from the served

37
00:02:16,576 --> 00:02:19,751
episodes, reads what's committed on Monad, and writes a

38
00:02:19,781 --> 00:02:21,642
verdict per task on chain.

39
00:02:22,773 --> 00:02:24,791
Its verdict: uncommitted.

40
00:02:24,821 --> 00:02:27,674
The episodes are served, but no root is committed yet,

41
00:02:27,704 --> 00:02:31,345
and CRE says so on chain, beside the data.

42
00:02:32,025 --> 00:02:34,886
Operators ranked by what they earned, agents by what

43
00:02:34,916 --> 00:02:35,860
they bought.

44
00:02:38,025 --> 00:02:40,781
And the network page reads Monad and Ethereum side by

45
00:02:40,811 --> 00:02:45,553
side, live. Thenar: people teach robots, own the data,

46
00:02:45,583 --> 00:02:47,154
and get paid on Monad.

